window.PHARM_BANK=[{"id":"pharm-001","concept":"Pharmacokinetics","stem":"Which process describes movement of a drug from its site of administration into the bloodstream?","choices":["Absorption","Distribution","Metabolism","Excretion"],"answer":0,"why":"Absorption is the transfer of a drug from its administration site into systemic circulation.","zh":"吸收是药物从给药部位进入体循环的过程。","pearl":"ADME begins with absorption.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Distribution” is incorrect here. Distribution is movement of drug from the bloodstream into tissues and body fluids. In this question, Absorption is the transfer of a drug from its administration site into systemic circulation.","zh":"“Distribution”在此题中不正确。分布是药物从血液进入组织和体液。 本题的正确原则是：吸收是药物从给药部位进入体循环的过程。"},{"en":"“Metabolism” is incorrect here. Metabolism is enzymatic chemical alteration of a drug, mainly in the liver. In this question, Absorption is the transfer of a drug from its administration site into systemic circulation.","zh":"“Metabolism”在此题中不正确。代谢是药物的酶促化学改变，主要发生在肝脏。 本题的正确原则是：吸收是药物从给药部位进入体循环的过程。"},{"en":"“Excretion” is incorrect here. Excretion is removal of drug or metabolites, commonly through the kidneys. In this question, Absorption is the transfer of a drug from its administration site into systemic circulation.","zh":"“Excretion”在此题中不正确。排泄是清除药物或其代谢物，通常经肾脏完成。 本题的正确原则是：吸收是药物从给药部位进入体循环的过程。"}]},{"id":"pharm-002","concept":"Pharmacokinetics","stem":"A drug undergoes extensive first-pass metabolism. Which route most directly avoids this effect?","choices":["Oral","Sublingual","Swallowed capsule","Enteric-coated tablet"],"answer":1,"why":"Sublingual drugs enter systemic circulation through oral mucosa and largely bypass initial hepatic first-pass metabolism.","zh":"舌下给药经口腔黏膜进入体循环，可大体避开肝脏首过效应。","pearl":"Sublingual is rapid and bypasses first pass.","rationales":[{"en":"“Oral” is incorrect here. Orally swallowed drugs commonly pass through the liver before reaching systemic circulation. In this question, Sublingual drugs enter systemic circulation through oral mucosa and largely bypass initial hepatic first-pass metabolism.","zh":"“Oral”在此题中不正确。口服吞咽药物通常在进入体循环前先经过肝脏。 本题的正确原则是：舌下给药经口腔黏膜进入体循环，可大体避开肝脏首过效应。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Swallowed capsule” is incorrect here. A swallowed capsule follows the gastrointestinal route and remains subject to first-pass metabolism. In this question, Sublingual drugs enter systemic circulation through oral mucosa and largely bypass initial hepatic first-pass metabolism.","zh":"“Swallowed capsule”在此题中不正确。吞服胶囊经胃肠道吸收，仍会受到首过代谢影响。 本题的正确原则是：舌下给药经口腔黏膜进入体循环，可大体避开肝脏首过效应。"},{"en":"“Enteric-coated tablet” is incorrect here. Enteric coating delays dissolution until the intestine; it does not bypass hepatic first-pass metabolism. In this question, Sublingual drugs enter systemic circulation through oral mucosa and largely bypass initial hepatic first-pass metabolism.","zh":"“Enteric-coated tablet”在此题中不正确。肠溶包衣只延迟至肠道溶解，并不能绕过肝脏首过代谢。 本题的正确原则是：舌下给药经口腔黏膜进入体循环，可大体避开肝脏首过效应。"}]},{"id":"pharm-003","concept":"Pharmacokinetics","stem":"A medication has a long half-life. What is the most likely consequence?","choices":["It is eliminated very rapidly","It may accumulate with repeated dosing","It cannot enter tissues","It must be given sublingually"],"answer":1,"why":"A long half-life means slower elimination, so repeated doses can accumulate until steady state is reached.","zh":"半衰期长表示消除较慢，重复给药时可能蓄积，直到达到稳态。","pearl":"Long half-life often means longer dosing intervals and greater accumulation risk.","rationales":[{"en":"“It is eliminated very rapidly” is incorrect here. A long half-life means slow elimination, not rapid elimination. In this question, A long half-life means slower elimination, so repeated doses can accumulate until steady state is reached.","zh":"“It is eliminated very rapidly”在此题中不正确。长半衰期表示清除较慢，而不是快速清除。 本题的正确原则是：半衰期长表示消除较慢，重复给药时可能蓄积，直到达到稳态。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“It cannot enter tissues” is incorrect here. Tissue entry concerns distribution and is not determined simply by a long half-life. In this question, A long half-life means slower elimination, so repeated doses can accumulate until steady state is reached.","zh":"“It cannot enter tissues”在此题中不正确。进入组织属于分布问题，不能仅由半衰期长短决定。 本题的正确原则是：半衰期长表示消除较慢，重复给药时可能蓄积，直到达到稳态。"},{"en":"“It must be given sublingually” is incorrect here. Half-life does not dictate that a drug must use the sublingual route. In this question, A long half-life means slower elimination, so repeated doses can accumulate until steady state is reached.","zh":"“It must be given sublingually”在此题中不正确。半衰期并不决定药物必须舌下给药。 本题的正确原则是：半衰期长表示消除较慢，重复给药时可能蓄积，直到达到稳态。"}]},{"id":"pharm-004","concept":"Pharmacodynamics","stem":"A drug binds to a receptor and produces a response. It is acting as a:","choices":["Antagonist","Agonist","Chelator","Placebo"],"answer":1,"why":"An agonist binds to a receptor and activates it to produce a biologic response.","zh":"激动剂与受体结合并激活受体，从而产生生物效应。","pearl":"Agonists activate; antagonists block.","rationales":[{"en":"“Antagonist” is incorrect here. An antagonist binds a receptor but blocks or reduces receptor activation. In this question, An agonist binds to a receptor and activates it to produce a biologic response.","zh":"“Antagonist”在此题中不正确。拮抗剂与受体结合，但阻断或减弱受体激活。 本题的正确原则是：激动剂与受体结合并激活受体，从而产生生物效应。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Chelator” is incorrect here. A chelator binds metal ions; it is not defined by receptor activation. In this question, An agonist binds to a receptor and activates it to produce a biologic response.","zh":"“Chelator”在此题中不正确。螯合剂与金属离子结合，并非通过激活受体发挥作用。 本题的正确原则是：激动剂与受体结合并激活受体，从而产生生物效应。"},{"en":"“Placebo” is incorrect here. A placebo lacks the specific active drug action being tested. In this question, An agonist binds to a receptor and activates it to produce a biologic response.","zh":"“Placebo”在此题中不正确。安慰剂不具有被测试药物的特异性药理作用。 本题的正确原则是：激动剂与受体结合并激活受体，从而产生生物效应。"}]},{"id":"pharm-005","concept":"Pharmacodynamics","stem":"Which term describes the amount of drug needed to produce a given effect?","choices":["Efficacy","Potency","Half-life","Bioavailability"],"answer":1,"why":"Potency refers to how much drug is required for an effect. Efficacy refers to the maximum effect a drug can produce.","zh":"效价强度表示产生特定效应所需的药量；效能表示药物可达到的最大效应。","pearl":"Potency is dose; efficacy is ceiling.","rationales":[{"en":"“Efficacy” is incorrect here. Efficacy is the maximum effect a drug can produce, not the dose required to produce it. In this question, Potency refers to how much drug is required for an effect. Efficacy refers to the maximum effect a drug can produce.","zh":"“Efficacy”在此题中不正确。效能是药物可产生的最大效应，而不是达到该效应所需剂量。 本题的正确原则是：效价强度表示产生特定效应所需的药量；效能表示药物可达到的最大效应。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Half-life” is incorrect here. Half-life is the time required for the drug concentration to decrease by half. In this question, Potency refers to how much drug is required for an effect. Efficacy refers to the maximum effect a drug can produce.","zh":"“Half-life”在此题中不正确。半衰期是药物浓度下降一半所需的时间。 本题的正确原则是：效价强度表示产生特定效应所需的药量；效能表示药物可达到的最大效应。"},{"en":"“Bioavailability” is incorrect here. Bioavailability is the fraction of an administered dose that reaches systemic circulation. In this question, Potency refers to how much drug is required for an effect. Efficacy refers to the maximum effect a drug can produce.","zh":"“Bioavailability”在此题中不正确。生物利用度是给药剂量中进入体循环的比例。 本题的正确原则是：效价强度表示产生特定效应所需的药量；效能表示药物可达到的最大效应。"}]},{"id":"pharm-006","concept":"Adverse Drug Reactions","stem":"A predictable, dose-related extension of a drug's normal action is classified as:","choices":["Type A adverse reaction","Type B adverse reaction","Allergy only","Idiosyncratic reaction only"],"answer":0,"why":"Type A reactions are augmented, predictable, and often dose-related. Type B reactions are unusual and less predictable.","zh":"A型不良反应通常是可预测、与剂量相关的药理作用增强。","pearl":"Type A = augmented and common; Type B = bizarre and uncommon.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Type B adverse reaction” is incorrect here. Type B reactions are uncommon, unpredictable, and not simply an extension of the usual dose-related action. In this question, Type A reactions are augmented, predictable, and often dose-related. Type B reactions are unusual and less predictable.","zh":"“Type B adverse reaction”在此题中不正确。B型不良反应少见且难以预测，并非正常药理作用的剂量延伸。 本题的正确原则是：A型不良反应通常是可预测、与剂量相关的药理作用增强。"},{"en":"“Allergy only” is incorrect here. Allergy is immune-mediated and is not the classification for every predictable dose-related adverse effect. In this question, Type A reactions are augmented, predictable, and often dose-related. Type B reactions are unusual and less predictable.","zh":"“Allergy only”在此题中不正确。过敏由免疫机制介导，不能用来概括所有可预测的剂量相关不良反应。 本题的正确原则是：A型不良反应通常是可预测、与剂量相关的药理作用增强。"},{"en":"“Idiosyncratic reaction only” is incorrect here. An idiosyncratic reaction is unusual and unpredictable rather than a typical dose-related effect. In this question, Type A reactions are augmented, predictable, and often dose-related. Type B reactions are unusual and less predictable.","zh":"“Idiosyncratic reaction only”在此题中不正确。特异质反应异常且难预测，并非典型剂量相关效应。 本题的正确原则是：A型不良反应通常是可预测、与剂量相关的药理作用增强。"}]},{"id":"pharm-007","concept":"Adverse Drug Reactions","stem":"Which finding most strongly suggests an immediate allergic reaction?","choices":["Dry mouth developing over months","Urticaria with wheezing shortly after a dose","Mild constipation","Metallic taste"],"answer":1,"why":"Rapid urticaria and wheezing suggest an immediate hypersensitivity reaction that can progress to anaphylaxis.","zh":"用药后迅速出现荨麻疹和喘鸣提示即刻型超敏反应，可能进展为过敏性休克。","pearl":"Hives plus airway symptoms is an emergency pattern.","rationales":[{"en":"“Dry mouth developing over months” is incorrect here. This is a possible adverse effect, but it does not indicate an immediate IgE-type allergic emergency. In this question, Rapid urticaria and wheezing suggest an immediate hypersensitivity reaction that can progress to anaphylaxis.","zh":"“Dry mouth developing over months”在此题中不正确。这可能是不良反应，但不提示即刻型IgE介导的过敏急症。 本题的正确原则是：用药后迅速出现荨麻疹和喘鸣提示即刻型超敏反应，可能进展为过敏性休克。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Mild constipation” is incorrect here. This is a possible adverse effect, but it does not indicate an immediate IgE-type allergic emergency. In this question, Rapid urticaria and wheezing suggest an immediate hypersensitivity reaction that can progress to anaphylaxis.","zh":"“Mild constipation”在此题中不正确。这可能是不良反应，但不提示即刻型IgE介导的过敏急症。 本题的正确原则是：用药后迅速出现荨麻疹和喘鸣提示即刻型超敏反应，可能进展为过敏性休克。"},{"en":"“Metallic taste” is incorrect here. This is a possible adverse effect, but it does not indicate an immediate IgE-type allergic emergency. In this question, Rapid urticaria and wheezing suggest an immediate hypersensitivity reaction that can progress to anaphylaxis.","zh":"“Metallic taste”在此题中不正确。这可能是不良反应，但不提示即刻型IgE介导的过敏急症。 本题的正确原则是：用药后迅速出现荨麻疹和喘鸣提示即刻型超敏反应，可能进展为过敏性休克。"}]},{"id":"pharm-008","concept":"Autonomic Pharmacology","stem":"Stimulation of the sympathetic nervous system most commonly causes:","choices":["Decreased heart rate and bronchoconstriction","Increased heart rate and bronchodilation","Increased salivation and digestion","Pupil constriction"],"answer":1,"why":"Sympathetic activation prepares the body for action, increasing heart rate and dilating bronchi.","zh":"交感神经兴奋会提高心率并扩张支气管，使身体进入应激状态。","pearl":"Sympathetic = fight or flight.","rationales":[{"en":"“Decreased heart rate and bronchoconstriction” is incorrect here. This reflects parasympathetic rather than typical sympathetic stimulation. In this question, Sympathetic activation prepares the body for action, increasing heart rate and dilating bronchi.","zh":"“Decreased heart rate and bronchoconstriction”在此题中不正确。这更符合副交感神经作用，而不是典型交感神经兴奋。 本题的正确原则是：交感神经兴奋会提高心率并扩张支气管，使身体进入应激状态。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Increased salivation and digestion” is incorrect here. This reflects parasympathetic rather than typical sympathetic stimulation. In this question, Sympathetic activation prepares the body for action, increasing heart rate and dilating bronchi.","zh":"“Increased salivation and digestion”在此题中不正确。这更符合副交感神经作用，而不是典型交感神经兴奋。 本题的正确原则是：交感神经兴奋会提高心率并扩张支气管，使身体进入应激状态。"},{"en":"“Pupil constriction” is incorrect here. This reflects parasympathetic rather than typical sympathetic stimulation. In this question, Sympathetic activation prepares the body for action, increasing heart rate and dilating bronchi.","zh":"“Pupil constriction”在此题中不正确。这更符合副交感神经作用，而不是典型交感神经兴奋。 本题的正确原则是：交感神经兴奋会提高心率并扩张支气管，使身体进入应激状态。"}]},{"id":"pharm-009","concept":"Autonomic Pharmacology","stem":"An anticholinergic medication is most likely to cause:","choices":["Excess salivation","Xerostomia","Bradycardia with tearing","Diarrhea"],"answer":1,"why":"Blocking muscarinic cholinergic activity reduces salivary secretion and commonly causes dry mouth.","zh":"阻断毒蕈碱型胆碱能作用会减少唾液分泌，常导致口干。","pearl":"Anticholinergic effects are dry: dry mouth, blurred vision, urinary retention.","rationales":[{"en":"“Excess salivation” is incorrect here. Anticholinergic drugs reduce muscarinic activity, so secretions and gastrointestinal motility tend to decrease rather than increase. In this question, Blocking muscarinic cholinergic activity reduces salivary secretion and commonly causes dry mouth.","zh":"“Excess salivation”在此题中不正确。抗胆碱药降低毒蕈碱受体活动，因此分泌和胃肠蠕动通常减少而非增加。 本题的正确原则是：阻断毒蕈碱型胆碱能作用会减少唾液分泌，常导致口干。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Bradycardia with tearing” is incorrect here. Anticholinergic drugs reduce muscarinic activity, so secretions and gastrointestinal motility tend to decrease rather than increase. In this question, Blocking muscarinic cholinergic activity reduces salivary secretion and commonly causes dry mouth.","zh":"“Bradycardia with tearing”在此题中不正确。抗胆碱药降低毒蕈碱受体活动，因此分泌和胃肠蠕动通常减少而非增加。 本题的正确原则是：阻断毒蕈碱型胆碱能作用会减少唾液分泌，常导致口干。"},{"en":"“Diarrhea” is incorrect here. Anticholinergic drugs reduce muscarinic activity, so secretions and gastrointestinal motility tend to decrease rather than increase. In this question, Blocking muscarinic cholinergic activity reduces salivary secretion and commonly causes dry mouth.","zh":"“Diarrhea”在此题中不正确。抗胆碱药降低毒蕈碱受体活动，因此分泌和胃肠蠕动通常减少而非增加。 本题的正确原则是：阻断毒蕈碱型胆碱能作用会减少唾液分泌，常导致口干。"}]},{"id":"pharm-010","concept":"Cardiovascular Drugs","stem":"A client taking a nonselective beta blocker may have an enhanced pressor response to:","choices":["Epinephrine","Acetaminophen","Amoxicillin","Nystatin"],"answer":0,"why":"Nonselective beta blockade can leave alpha-mediated vasoconstriction relatively unopposed when epinephrine is administered.","zh":"非选择性β受体阻滞剂与肾上腺素合用时，α介导的血管收缩可能相对无对抗而增强。","pearl":"Use vasoconstrictors cautiously with nonselective beta blockers.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Acetaminophen” is incorrect here. Acetaminophen is an analgesic and antipyretic with little anti-inflammatory activity at usual doses. In this question, Nonselective beta blockade can leave alpha-mediated vasoconstriction relatively unopposed when epinephrine is administered.","zh":"“Acetaminophen”在此题中不正确。对乙酰氨基酚具有镇痛和退热作用，常用剂量下抗炎作用很弱。 本题的正确原则是：非选择性β受体阻滞剂与肾上腺素合用时，α介导的血管收缩可能相对无对抗而增强。"},{"en":"“Amoxicillin” is incorrect here. Amoxicillin is a penicillin antibiotic and does not produce the adrenergic interaction described. In this question, Nonselective beta blockade can leave alpha-mediated vasoconstriction relatively unopposed when epinephrine is administered.","zh":"“Amoxicillin”在此题中不正确。阿莫西林属于青霉素类抗生素，不会产生题干所述肾上腺素能相互作用。 本题的正确原则是：非选择性β受体阻滞剂与肾上腺素合用时，α介导的血管收缩可能相对无对抗而增强。"},{"en":"“Nystatin” is incorrect here. Nystatin is an antifungal used mainly for Candida infections. In this question, Nonselective beta blockade can leave alpha-mediated vasoconstriction relatively unopposed when epinephrine is administered.","zh":"“Nystatin”在此题中不正确。制霉菌素是主要用于念珠菌感染的抗真菌药。 本题的正确原则是：非选择性β受体阻滞剂与肾上腺素合用时，α介导的血管收缩可能相对无对抗而增强。"}]},{"id":"pharm-011","concept":"Cardiovascular Drugs","stem":"Which oral finding is classically associated with some calcium channel blockers?","choices":["Black hairy tongue","Gingival enlargement","Aphthous ulcers only","Enamel hypoplasia"],"answer":1,"why":"Some calcium channel blockers, especially certain agents such as nifedipine, may contribute to gingival enlargement.","zh":"部分钙通道阻滞剂，尤其某些药物如硝苯地平，可能引起牙龈增生。","pearl":"Medication, plaque, and inflammation can combine to worsen enlargement.","rationales":[{"en":"“Black hairy tongue” is incorrect here. This is not the classic oral adverse effect associated with calcium channel blockers. In this question, Some calcium channel blockers, especially certain agents such as nifedipine, may contribute to gingival enlargement.","zh":"“Black hairy tongue”在此题中不正确。这不是钙通道阻滞剂的经典口腔不良反应。 本题的正确原则是：部分钙通道阻滞剂，尤其某些药物如硝苯地平，可能引起牙龈增生。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Aphthous ulcers only” is incorrect here. This is not the classic oral adverse effect associated with calcium channel blockers. In this question, Some calcium channel blockers, especially certain agents such as nifedipine, may contribute to gingival enlargement.","zh":"“Aphthous ulcers only”在此题中不正确。这不是钙通道阻滞剂的经典口腔不良反应。 本题的正确原则是：部分钙通道阻滞剂，尤其某些药物如硝苯地平，可能引起牙龈增生。"},{"en":"“Enamel hypoplasia” is incorrect here. This is not the classic oral adverse effect associated with calcium channel blockers. In this question, Some calcium channel blockers, especially certain agents such as nifedipine, may contribute to gingival enlargement.","zh":"“Enamel hypoplasia”在此题中不正确。这不是钙通道阻滞剂的经典口腔不良反应。 本题的正确原则是：部分钙通道阻滞剂，尤其某些药物如硝苯地平，可能引起牙龈增生。"}]},{"id":"pharm-012","concept":"Cardiovascular Drugs","stem":"A client taking an ACE inhibitor develops a persistent dry cough. This is:","choices":["A recognized class effect","Evidence of opioid toxicity","A sign of hypoglycemia","Always an allergy"],"answer":0,"why":"A persistent dry cough is a well-known adverse effect of ACE inhibitors.","zh":"持续干咳是ACE抑制剂常见的不良反应。","pearl":"ACE inhibitors can also rarely cause angioedema.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Evidence of opioid toxicity” is incorrect here. The dry cough is a recognized ACE-inhibitor class effect and does not by itself establish this alternative. In this question, A persistent dry cough is a well-known adverse effect of ACE inhibitors.","zh":"“Evidence of opioid toxicity”在此题中不正确。干咳是ACE抑制剂公认的类别效应，不能据此判定为该选项。 本题的正确原则是：持续干咳是ACE抑制剂常见的不良反应。"},{"en":"“A sign of hypoglycemia” is incorrect here. Hypoglycemia causes adrenergic and neuroglycopenic signs such as sweating, shaking, and confusion. In this question, A persistent dry cough is a well-known adverse effect of ACE inhibitors.","zh":"“A sign of hypoglycemia”在此题中不正确。低血糖可引起出汗、发抖、意识混乱等交感神经和神经缺糖症状。 本题的正确原则是：持续干咳是ACE抑制剂常见的不良反应。"},{"en":"“Always an allergy” is incorrect here. The dry cough is a recognized ACE-inhibitor class effect and does not by itself establish this alternative. In this question, A persistent dry cough is a well-known adverse effect of ACE inhibitors.","zh":"“Always an allergy”在此题中不正确。干咳是ACE抑制剂公认的类别效应，不能据此判定为该选项。 本题的正确原则是：持续干咳是ACE抑制剂常见的不良反应。"}]},{"id":"pharm-013","concept":"Cardiovascular Drugs","stem":"A client using nitroglycerin for angina should be asked about recent use of:","choices":["Phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors","Penicillin","Acetaminophen","Topical fluoride"],"answer":0,"why":"Combining nitrates with phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors can cause profound, dangerous hypotension.","zh":"硝酸酯类与PDE-5抑制剂合用可导致严重低血压。","pearl":"Nitrates plus PDE-5 inhibitors is a major contraindicated combination.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Penicillin” is incorrect here. This does not create the dangerous nitrate interaction caused by phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors. In this question, Combining nitrates with phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors can cause profound, dangerous hypotension.","zh":"“Penicillin”在此题中不正确。该物质不会产生PDE-5抑制剂与硝酸酯合用时的危险相互作用。 本题的正确原则是：硝酸酯类与PDE-5抑制剂合用可导致严重低血压。"},{"en":"“Acetaminophen” is incorrect here. Acetaminophen is an analgesic and antipyretic with little anti-inflammatory activity at usual doses. In this question, Combining nitrates with phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors can cause profound, dangerous hypotension.","zh":"“Acetaminophen”在此题中不正确。对乙酰氨基酚具有镇痛和退热作用，常用剂量下抗炎作用很弱。 本题的正确原则是：硝酸酯类与PDE-5抑制剂合用可导致严重低血压。"},{"en":"“Topical fluoride” is incorrect here. Topical fluoride acts locally to prevent caries and is not a sympathomimetic interaction concern. In this question, Combining nitrates with phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors can cause profound, dangerous hypotension.","zh":"“Topical fluoride”在此题中不正确。局部氟化物用于局部防龋，并非拟交感神经药相互作用问题。 本题的正确原则是：硝酸酯类与PDE-5抑制剂合用可导致严重低血压。"}]},{"id":"pharm-014","concept":"Anticoagulants & Antiplatelets","stem":"A client takes warfarin. Which test is commonly used to monitor its anticoagulant effect?","choices":["INR","HbA1c","Creatinine clearance only","Peak flow"],"answer":0,"why":"The international normalized ratio (INR) is used to monitor warfarin therapy.","zh":"国际标准化比值（INR）用于监测华法林治疗。","pearl":"Warfarin monitoring = INR.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“HbA1c” is incorrect here. HbA1c reflects average glycemic control over the preceding months, not warfarin anticoagulation. In this question, The international normalized ratio (INR) is used to monitor warfarin therapy.","zh":"“HbA1c”在此题中不正确。糖化血红蛋白反映过去数月的平均血糖控制，并不监测华法林抗凝作用。 本题的正确原则是：国际标准化比值（INR）用于监测华法林治疗。"},{"en":"“Creatinine clearance only” is incorrect here. This option describes a different condition, drug action, or clinical use and does not match the mechanism or safety issue tested here. In this question, The international normalized ratio (INR) is used to monitor warfarin therapy.","zh":"“Creatinine clearance only”在此题中不正确。该选项描述的是不同的疾病、药物作用或临床用途，与本题考查的机制或安全问题不符。 本题的正确原则是：国际标准化比值（INR）用于监测华法林治疗。"},{"en":"“Peak flow” is incorrect here. Peak expiratory flow assesses airflow limitation in asthma, not anticoagulation. In this question, The international normalized ratio (INR) is used to monitor warfarin therapy.","zh":"“Peak flow”在此题中不正确。呼气峰流速用于评估哮喘气流受限，不用于监测抗凝。 本题的正确原则是：国际标准化比值（INR）用于监测华法林治疗。"}]},{"id":"pharm-015","concept":"Anticoagulants & Antiplatelets","stem":"What is the best general principle before invasive dental hygiene care for a client taking an anticoagulant?","choices":["Tell the client to stop it automatically","Assess bleeding risk and coordinate when needed; do not independently discontinue the drug","Double the dose after treatment","Ignore the medication"],"answer":1,"why":"Stopping anticoagulants without prescriber direction can increase thromboembolic risk. Care should be based on procedure risk, current status, and consultation when indicated.","zh":"未经处方医生指导自行停用抗凝药会增加血栓风险。应根据操作出血风险和患者情况决定，并在需要时会诊。","pearl":"Never independently order a client to stop anticoagulant therapy.","rationales":[{"en":"“Tell the client to stop it automatically” is incorrect here. Anticoagulant therapy should not be independently changed by the dental hygienist; risk assessment and consultation are required when indicated. In this question, Stopping anticoagulants without prescriber direction can increase thromboembolic risk. Care should be based on procedure risk, current status, and consultation when indicated.","zh":"“Tell the client to stop it automatically”在此题中不正确。牙科保健师不应自行更改抗凝治疗；应评估风险并在需要时会诊。 本题的正确原则是：未经处方医生指导自行停用抗凝药会增加血栓风险。应根据操作出血风险和患者情况决定，并在需要时会诊。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Double the dose after treatment” is incorrect here. Anticoagulant therapy should not be independently changed by the dental hygienist; risk assessment and consultation are required when indicated. In this question, Stopping anticoagulants without prescriber direction can increase thromboembolic risk. Care should be based on procedure risk, current status, and consultation when indicated.","zh":"“Double the dose after treatment”在此题中不正确。牙科保健师不应自行更改抗凝治疗；应评估风险并在需要时会诊。 本题的正确原则是：未经处方医生指导自行停用抗凝药会增加血栓风险。应根据操作出血风险和患者情况决定，并在需要时会诊。"},{"en":"“Ignore the medication” is incorrect here. Ignoring anticoagulation can miss clinically important bleeding and drug-interaction risks. In this question, Stopping anticoagulants without prescriber direction can increase thromboembolic risk. Care should be based on procedure risk, current status, and consultation when indicated.","zh":"“Ignore the medication”在此题中不正确。忽视抗凝治疗会漏掉重要出血和药物相互作用风险。 本题的正确原则是：未经处方医生指导自行停用抗凝药会增加血栓风险。应根据操作出血风险和患者情况决定，并在需要时会诊。"}]},{"id":"pharm-016","concept":"Anticoagulants & Antiplatelets","stem":"Which medication irreversibly inhibits platelet function for the life of the platelet?","choices":["Aspirin","Acetaminophen","Amoxicillin","Lidocaine"],"answer":0,"why":"Aspirin irreversibly inhibits platelet cyclooxygenase, affecting platelet function for the platelet lifespan.","zh":"阿司匹林不可逆抑制血小板环氧化酶，其影响持续至血小板寿命结束。","pearl":"Aspirin is antiplatelet, not an anticoagulant.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Acetaminophen” is incorrect here. Acetaminophen is an analgesic and antipyretic with little anti-inflammatory activity at usual doses. In this question, Aspirin irreversibly inhibits platelet cyclooxygenase, affecting platelet function for the platelet lifespan.","zh":"“Acetaminophen”在此题中不正确。对乙酰氨基酚具有镇痛和退热作用，常用剂量下抗炎作用很弱。 本题的正确原则是：阿司匹林不可逆抑制血小板环氧化酶，其影响持续至血小板寿命结束。"},{"en":"“Amoxicillin” is incorrect here. Amoxicillin is a penicillin antibiotic and does not produce the adrenergic interaction described. In this question, Aspirin irreversibly inhibits platelet cyclooxygenase, affecting platelet function for the platelet lifespan.","zh":"“Amoxicillin”在此题中不正确。阿莫西林属于青霉素类抗生素，不会产生题干所述肾上腺素能相互作用。 本题的正确原则是：阿司匹林不可逆抑制血小板环氧化酶，其影响持续至血小板寿命结束。"},{"en":"“Lidocaine” is incorrect here. This option describes a different condition, drug action, or clinical use and does not match the mechanism or safety issue tested here. In this question, Aspirin irreversibly inhibits platelet cyclooxygenase, affecting platelet function for the platelet lifespan.","zh":"“Lidocaine”在此题中不正确。该选项描述的是不同的疾病、药物作用或临床用途，与本题考查的机制或安全问题不符。 本题的正确原则是：阿司匹林不可逆抑制血小板环氧化酶，其影响持续至血小板寿命结束。"}]},{"id":"pharm-017","concept":"Analgesics","stem":"Which analgesic has minimal anti-inflammatory activity at usual doses?","choices":["Ibuprofen","Naproxen","Acetaminophen","Ketorolac"],"answer":2,"why":"Acetaminophen is analgesic and antipyretic but has little clinically useful anti-inflammatory effect at usual doses.","zh":"对乙酰氨基酚具有镇痛和退热作用，但常用剂量下抗炎作用很弱。","pearl":"Acetaminophen is not an NSAID.","rationales":[{"en":"“Ibuprofen” is incorrect here. Ibuprofen is an NSAID with analgesic, antipyretic, and anti-inflammatory effects. In this question, Acetaminophen is analgesic and antipyretic but has little clinically useful anti-inflammatory effect at usual doses.","zh":"“Ibuprofen”在此题中不正确。布洛芬是具有镇痛、退热和抗炎作用的非甾体抗炎药。 本题的正确原则是：对乙酰氨基酚具有镇痛和退热作用，但常用剂量下抗炎作用很弱。"},{"en":"“Naproxen” is incorrect here. Naproxen is an NSAID with meaningful anti-inflammatory activity. In this question, Acetaminophen is analgesic and antipyretic but has little clinically useful anti-inflammatory effect at usual doses.","zh":"“Naproxen”在此题中不正确。萘普生是具有明显抗炎作用的非甾体抗炎药。 本题的正确原则是：对乙酰氨基酚具有镇痛和退热作用，但常用剂量下抗炎作用很弱。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Ketorolac” is incorrect here. Ketorolac is a potent NSAID analgesic and retains anti-inflammatory activity. In this question, Acetaminophen is analgesic and antipyretic but has little clinically useful anti-inflammatory effect at usual doses.","zh":"“Ketorolac”在此题中不正确。酮咯酸是强效非甾体镇痛药，也具有抗炎作用。 本题的正确原则是：对乙酰氨基酚具有镇痛和退热作用，但常用剂量下抗炎作用很弱。"}]},{"id":"pharm-018","concept":"Analgesics","stem":"A major toxicity concern with excessive acetaminophen use is:","choices":["Hepatic injury","Gingival enlargement","Bronchodilation","Hyperthyroidism"],"answer":0,"why":"Acetaminophen overdose can cause severe hepatotoxicity, especially when total daily dose is exceeded or alcohol misuse is present.","zh":"过量使用对乙酰氨基酚可导致严重肝损伤，尤其在超过每日总量或合并大量饮酒时。","pearl":"Check combination products to avoid hidden acetaminophen.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Gingival enlargement” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Acetaminophen overdose can cause severe hepatotoxicity, especially when total daily dose is exceeded or alcohol misuse is present.","zh":"“Gingival enlargement”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：过量使用对乙酰氨基酚可导致严重肝损伤，尤其在超过每日总量或合并大量饮酒时。"},{"en":"“Bronchodilation” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Acetaminophen overdose can cause severe hepatotoxicity, especially when total daily dose is exceeded or alcohol misuse is present.","zh":"“Bronchodilation”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：过量使用对乙酰氨基酚可导致严重肝损伤，尤其在超过每日总量或合并大量饮酒时。"},{"en":"“Hyperthyroidism” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Acetaminophen overdose can cause severe hepatotoxicity, especially when total daily dose is exceeded or alcohol misuse is present.","zh":"“Hyperthyroidism”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：过量使用对乙酰氨基酚可导致严重肝损伤，尤其在超过每日总量或合并大量饮酒时。"}]},{"id":"pharm-019","concept":"Analgesics","stem":"NSAIDs primarily reduce pain and inflammation by inhibiting:","choices":["Cyclooxygenase and prostaglandin synthesis","Insulin secretion","Histamine release only","Acetylcholine breakdown"],"answer":0,"why":"NSAIDs inhibit cyclooxygenase enzymes, reducing prostaglandin production.","zh":"非甾体抗炎药通过抑制环氧化酶，减少前列腺素生成。","pearl":"Less prostaglandin means less pain, fever, and inflammation, but also less gastric and renal protection.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Insulin secretion” is incorrect here. Insulin secretion regulates glucose metabolism and is not the primary target of NSAIDs. In this question, NSAIDs inhibit cyclooxygenase enzymes, reducing prostaglandin production.","zh":"“Insulin secretion”在此题中不正确。胰岛素分泌调节葡萄糖代谢，并非非甾体抗炎药的主要靶点。 本题的正确原则是：非甾体抗炎药通过抑制环氧化酶，减少前列腺素生成。"},{"en":"“Histamine release only” is incorrect here. This option describes a different condition, drug action, or clinical use and does not match the mechanism or safety issue tested here. In this question, NSAIDs inhibit cyclooxygenase enzymes, reducing prostaglandin production.","zh":"“Histamine release only”在此题中不正确。该选项描述的是不同的疾病、药物作用或临床用途，与本题考查的机制或安全问题不符。 本题的正确原则是：非甾体抗炎药通过抑制环氧化酶，减少前列腺素生成。"},{"en":"“Acetylcholine breakdown” is incorrect here. Acetylcholine breakdown is mediated by cholinesterases and is unrelated to the principal NSAID mechanism. In this question, NSAIDs inhibit cyclooxygenase enzymes, reducing prostaglandin production.","zh":"“Acetylcholine breakdown”在此题中不正确。乙酰胆碱由胆碱酯酶分解，与非甾体抗炎药的主要机制无关。 本题的正确原则是：非甾体抗炎药通过抑制环氧化酶，减少前列腺素生成。"}]},{"id":"pharm-020","concept":"Analgesics","stem":"Which client requires particular caution with NSAID use?","choices":["A client with a history of peptic ulcer and renal disease","A client with a healed paper cut","A client using fluoride toothpaste","A client with a composite restoration"],"answer":0,"why":"NSAIDs can increase gastrointestinal bleeding risk and impair renal function.","zh":"NSAIDs可增加胃肠道出血风险并损害肾功能。","pearl":"Think stomach, kidneys, bleeding, and some asthma.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“A client with a healed paper cut” is incorrect here. This does not create the gastrointestinal, renal, bleeding, or hypersensitivity risk that makes NSAIDs concerning. In this question, NSAIDs can increase gastrointestinal bleeding risk and impair renal function.","zh":"“A client with a healed paper cut”在此题中不正确。该情况不会产生使非甾体抗炎药需谨慎使用的胃肠、肾脏、出血或超敏风险。 本题的正确原则是：NSAIDs可增加胃肠道出血风险并损害肾功能。"},{"en":"“A client using fluoride toothpaste” is incorrect here. This does not create the gastrointestinal, renal, bleeding, or hypersensitivity risk that makes NSAIDs concerning. In this question, NSAIDs can increase gastrointestinal bleeding risk and impair renal function.","zh":"“A client using fluoride toothpaste”在此题中不正确。该情况不会产生使非甾体抗炎药需谨慎使用的胃肠、肾脏、出血或超敏风险。 本题的正确原则是：NSAIDs可增加胃肠道出血风险并损害肾功能。"},{"en":"“A client with a composite restoration” is incorrect here. This does not create the gastrointestinal, renal, bleeding, or hypersensitivity risk that makes NSAIDs concerning. In this question, NSAIDs can increase gastrointestinal bleeding risk and impair renal function.","zh":"“A client with a composite restoration”在此题中不正确。该情况不会产生使非甾体抗炎药需谨慎使用的胃肠、肾脏、出血或超敏风险。 本题的正确原则是：NSAIDs可增加胃肠道出血风险并损害肾功能。"}]},{"id":"pharm-021","concept":"Opioids","stem":"Which cluster is most consistent with opioid overdose?","choices":["Mydriasis, agitation, hypertension","Respiratory depression, decreased consciousness, pinpoint pupils","Diarrhea, tearing, yawning","Hyperactivity and insomnia"],"answer":1,"why":"The classic opioid toxicity triad includes respiratory depression, reduced consciousness, and miosis.","zh":"阿片类药物中毒经典三联征为呼吸抑制、意识下降和瞳孔缩小。","pearl":"Naloxone reverses opioid effects but may require repeat dosing.","rationales":[{"en":"“Mydriasis, agitation, hypertension” is incorrect here. This pattern is more consistent with stimulant effects or opioid withdrawal than opioid overdose. In this question, The classic opioid toxicity triad includes respiratory depression, reduced consciousness, and miosis.","zh":"“Mydriasis, agitation, hypertension”在此题中不正确。该表现更符合兴奋剂作用或阿片戒断，而不是阿片过量。 本题的正确原则是：阿片类药物中毒经典三联征为呼吸抑制、意识下降和瞳孔缩小。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Diarrhea, tearing, yawning” is incorrect here. Anticholinergic drugs reduce muscarinic activity, so secretions and gastrointestinal motility tend to decrease rather than increase. In this question, The classic opioid toxicity triad includes respiratory depression, reduced consciousness, and miosis.","zh":"“Diarrhea, tearing, yawning”在此题中不正确。抗胆碱药降低毒蕈碱受体活动，因此分泌和胃肠蠕动通常减少而非增加。 本题的正确原则是：阿片类药物中毒经典三联征为呼吸抑制、意识下降和瞳孔缩小。"},{"en":"“Hyperactivity and insomnia” is incorrect here. This pattern is more consistent with stimulant effects or opioid withdrawal than opioid overdose. In this question, The classic opioid toxicity triad includes respiratory depression, reduced consciousness, and miosis.","zh":"“Hyperactivity and insomnia”在此题中不正确。该表现更符合兴奋剂作用或阿片戒断，而不是阿片过量。 本题的正确原则是：阿片类药物中毒经典三联征为呼吸抑制、意识下降和瞳孔缩小。"}]},{"id":"pharm-022","concept":"Opioids","stem":"Concurrent use of opioids and benzodiazepines increases the risk of:","choices":["Severe CNS and respiratory depression","Improved alertness","Gingival enlargement","Hyperglycemia only"],"answer":0,"why":"Both depress the central nervous system, producing additive sedation and respiratory depression.","zh":"阿片类与苯二氮䓬类均抑制中枢神经系统，合用会增加镇静和呼吸抑制风险。","pearl":"Two sedatives can become far more dangerous than either alone.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Improved alertness” is incorrect here. Combining opioids and benzodiazepines produces additive CNS depression, not this effect. In this question, Both depress the central nervous system, producing additive sedation and respiratory depression.","zh":"“Improved alertness”在此题中不正确。阿片类与苯二氮卓类合用会产生叠加性中枢抑制，而不是该效应。 本题的正确原则是：阿片类与苯二氮䓬类均抑制中枢神经系统，合用会增加镇静和呼吸抑制风险。"},{"en":"“Gingival enlargement” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Both depress the central nervous system, producing additive sedation and respiratory depression.","zh":"“Gingival enlargement”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：阿片类与苯二氮䓬类均抑制中枢神经系统，合用会增加镇静和呼吸抑制风险。"},{"en":"“Hyperglycemia only” is incorrect here. Combining opioids and benzodiazepines produces additive CNS depression, not this effect. In this question, Both depress the central nervous system, producing additive sedation and respiratory depression.","zh":"“Hyperglycemia only”在此题中不正确。阿片类与苯二氮卓类合用会产生叠加性中枢抑制，而不是该效应。 本题的正确原则是：阿片类与苯二氮䓬类均抑制中枢神经系统，合用会增加镇静和呼吸抑制风险。"}]},{"id":"pharm-023","concept":"Antibiotics","stem":"Amoxicillin belongs to which antibiotic class?","choices":["Penicillins","Macrolides","Tetracyclines","Fluoroquinolones"],"answer":0,"why":"Amoxicillin is a beta-lactam penicillin antibiotic.","zh":"阿莫西林属于β-内酰胺类青霉素抗生素。","pearl":"Penicillins inhibit bacterial cell-wall synthesis.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Macrolides” is incorrect here. Macrolides include drugs such as azithromycin and clarithromycin, not amoxicillin. In this question, Amoxicillin is a beta-lactam penicillin antibiotic.","zh":"“Macrolides”在此题中不正确。大环内酯类包括阿奇霉素和克拉霉素等，不包括阿莫西林。 本题的正确原则是：阿莫西林属于β-内酰胺类青霉素抗生素。"},{"en":"“Tetracyclines” is incorrect here. Tetracyclines are a separate antibiotic class associated with effects such as tooth discoloration during development. In this question, Amoxicillin is a beta-lactam penicillin antibiotic.","zh":"“Tetracyclines”在此题中不正确。四环素类是另一类抗生素，牙齿发育期使用可导致着色。 本题的正确原则是：阿莫西林属于β-内酰胺类青霉素抗生素。"},{"en":"“Fluoroquinolones” is incorrect here. Fluoroquinolones are a distinct antibiotic class that inhibits bacterial DNA enzymes. In this question, Amoxicillin is a beta-lactam penicillin antibiotic.","zh":"“Fluoroquinolones”在此题中不正确。氟喹诺酮类是抑制细菌DNA相关酶的独立抗生素类别。 本题的正确原则是：阿莫西林属于β-内酰胺类青霉素抗生素。"}]},{"id":"pharm-024","concept":"Antibiotics","stem":"A client reports immediate anaphylaxis after penicillin. Which antibiotic requires careful cross-reactivity consideration?","choices":["A cephalosporin","Metronidazole","Nystatin","Acyclovir"],"answer":0,"why":"Cephalosporins share beta-lactam structural features with penicillins, so the nature and severity of the previous reaction must be considered.","zh":"头孢菌素与青霉素同属β-内酰胺结构，因此必须考虑既往反应的类型和严重程度。","pearl":"Clarify the reaction, not merely the word allergy.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Metronidazole” is incorrect here. Metronidazole is active against many anaerobes and protozoa and is not a beta-lactam. In this question, Cephalosporins share beta-lactam structural features with penicillins, so the nature and severity of the previous reaction must be considered.","zh":"“Metronidazole”在此题中不正确。甲硝唑对多种厌氧菌和原虫有效，并非β-内酰胺类。 本题的正确原则是：头孢菌素与青霉素同属β-内酰胺结构，因此必须考虑既往反应的类型和严重程度。"},{"en":"“Nystatin” is incorrect here. Nystatin is an antifungal used mainly for Candida infections. In this question, Cephalosporins share beta-lactam structural features with penicillins, so the nature and severity of the previous reaction must be considered.","zh":"“Nystatin”在此题中不正确。制霉菌素是主要用于念珠菌感染的抗真菌药。 本题的正确原则是：头孢菌素与青霉素同属β-内酰胺结构，因此必须考虑既往反应的类型和严重程度。"},{"en":"“Acyclovir” is incorrect here. Acyclovir is an antiviral active mainly against herpes viruses. In this question, Cephalosporins share beta-lactam structural features with penicillins, so the nature and severity of the previous reaction must be considered.","zh":"“Acyclovir”在此题中不正确。阿昔洛韦是主要针对疱疹病毒的抗病毒药。 本题的正确原则是：头孢菌素与青霉素同属β-内酰胺结构，因此必须考虑既往反应的类型和严重程度。"}]},{"id":"pharm-025","concept":"Antibiotics","stem":"Which adverse effect is particularly associated with clindamycin?","choices":["C. difficile-associated colitis","Severe hypoglycemia in every client","Gingival enlargement","Bronchodilation"],"answer":0,"why":"Clindamycin is strongly associated with antibiotic-associated diarrhea and C. difficile colitis.","zh":"克林霉素与抗生素相关性腹泻及艰难梭菌性结肠炎密切相关。","pearl":"Severe or persistent diarrhea after antibiotics needs prompt assessment.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Severe hypoglycemia in every client” is incorrect here. Hypoglycemia causes adrenergic and neuroglycopenic signs such as sweating, shaking, and confusion. In this question, Clindamycin is strongly associated with antibiotic-associated diarrhea and C. difficile colitis.","zh":"“Severe hypoglycemia in every client”在此题中不正确。低血糖可引起出汗、发抖、意识混乱等交感神经和神经缺糖症状。 本题的正确原则是：克林霉素与抗生素相关性腹泻及艰难梭菌性结肠炎密切相关。"},{"en":"“Gingival enlargement” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Clindamycin is strongly associated with antibiotic-associated diarrhea and C. difficile colitis.","zh":"“Gingival enlargement”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：克林霉素与抗生素相关性腹泻及艰难梭菌性结肠炎密切相关。"},{"en":"“Bronchodilation” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Clindamycin is strongly associated with antibiotic-associated diarrhea and C. difficile colitis.","zh":"“Bronchodilation”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：克林霉素与抗生素相关性腹泻及艰难梭菌性结肠炎密切相关。"}]},{"id":"pharm-026","concept":"Antibiotics","stem":"Metronidazole should generally not be combined with alcohol because of the risk of:","choices":["A disulfiram-like reaction","Permanent tooth staining","Profound hypoglycemia in all clients","Opioid withdrawal"],"answer":0,"why":"Alcohol with metronidazole may produce flushing, nausea, vomiting, headache, and other disulfiram-like effects.","zh":"甲硝唑与酒精同用可能引起潮红、恶心、呕吐、头痛等双硫仑样反应。","pearl":"Metronidazole: think anaerobes and avoid alcohol.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Permanent tooth staining” is incorrect here. This is not the alcohol-related reaction associated with metronidazole. In this question, Alcohol with metronidazole may produce flushing, nausea, vomiting, headache, and other disulfiram-like effects.","zh":"“Permanent tooth staining”在此题中不正确。这不是甲硝唑与酒精相关的典型反应。 本题的正确原则是：甲硝唑与酒精同用可能引起潮红、恶心、呕吐、头痛等双硫仑样反应。"},{"en":"“Profound hypoglycemia in all clients” is incorrect here. Hypoglycemia causes adrenergic and neuroglycopenic signs such as sweating, shaking, and confusion. In this question, Alcohol with metronidazole may produce flushing, nausea, vomiting, headache, and other disulfiram-like effects.","zh":"“Profound hypoglycemia in all clients”在此题中不正确。低血糖可引起出汗、发抖、意识混乱等交感神经和神经缺糖症状。 本题的正确原则是：甲硝唑与酒精同用可能引起潮红、恶心、呕吐、头痛等双硫仑样反应。"},{"en":"“Opioid withdrawal” is incorrect here. This is not the alcohol-related reaction associated with metronidazole. In this question, Alcohol with metronidazole may produce flushing, nausea, vomiting, headache, and other disulfiram-like effects.","zh":"“Opioid withdrawal”在此题中不正确。这不是甲硝唑与酒精相关的典型反应。 本题的正确原则是：甲硝唑与酒精同用可能引起潮红、恶心、呕吐、头痛等双硫仑样反应。"}]},{"id":"pharm-027","concept":"Antibiotics","stem":"Tetracycline use during tooth development can cause:","choices":["Intrinsic tooth discoloration","Immediate gingival enlargement","Reversible calculus","Only dry mouth"],"answer":0,"why":"Tetracyclines can bind to developing mineralized tissues and cause intrinsic discoloration.","zh":"四环素可与发育中的矿化组织结合，导致内源性牙齿变色。","pearl":"Avoid tetracyclines during pregnancy and early tooth development when clinically applicable.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Immediate gingival enlargement” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Tetracyclines can bind to developing mineralized tissues and cause intrinsic discoloration.","zh":"“Immediate gingival enlargement”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：四环素可与发育中的矿化组织结合，导致内源性牙齿变色。"},{"en":"“Reversible calculus” is incorrect here. This does not describe tetracycline incorporation into developing teeth and intrinsic discoloration. In this question, Tetracyclines can bind to developing mineralized tissues and cause intrinsic discoloration.","zh":"“Reversible calculus”在此题中不正确。这不能解释四环素进入发育中牙体组织并造成内源性着色。 本题的正确原则是：四环素可与发育中的矿化组织结合，导致内源性牙齿变色。"},{"en":"“Only dry mouth” is incorrect here. This does not describe tetracycline incorporation into developing teeth and intrinsic discoloration. In this question, Tetracyclines can bind to developing mineralized tissues and cause intrinsic discoloration.","zh":"“Only dry mouth”在此题中不正确。这不能解释四环素进入发育中牙体组织并造成内源性着色。 本题的正确原则是：四环素可与发育中的矿化组织结合，导致内源性牙齿变色。"}]},{"id":"pharm-028","concept":"Antibiotics","stem":"Why should broad-spectrum antibiotics not be used unnecessarily?","choices":["They promote resistance and disrupt normal flora","They always improve viral infections","They eliminate all adverse effects","They prevent every dental infection"],"answer":0,"why":"Unnecessary use promotes antimicrobial resistance and can disturb protective normal microbiota.","zh":"不必要使用广谱抗生素会促进耐药并破坏正常菌群。","pearl":"Antibiotic stewardship means the right drug only when truly indicated.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“They always improve viral infections” is incorrect here. Antibiotics do not treat viruses, eliminate all risks, or prevent every infection; unnecessary use instead selects for resistance. In this question, Unnecessary use promotes antimicrobial resistance and can disturb protective normal microbiota.","zh":"“They always improve viral infections”在此题中不正确。抗生素不能治疗病毒、消除所有风险或预防每种感染；不必要使用反而会选择耐药菌。 本题的正确原则是：不必要使用广谱抗生素会促进耐药并破坏正常菌群。"},{"en":"“They eliminate all adverse effects” is incorrect here. Antibiotics do not treat viruses, eliminate all risks, or prevent every infection; unnecessary use instead selects for resistance. In this question, Unnecessary use promotes antimicrobial resistance and can disturb protective normal microbiota.","zh":"“They eliminate all adverse effects”在此题中不正确。抗生素不能治疗病毒、消除所有风险或预防每种感染；不必要使用反而会选择耐药菌。 本题的正确原则是：不必要使用广谱抗生素会促进耐药并破坏正常菌群。"},{"en":"“They prevent every dental infection” is incorrect here. Antibiotics do not treat viruses, eliminate all risks, or prevent every infection; unnecessary use instead selects for resistance. In this question, Unnecessary use promotes antimicrobial resistance and can disturb protective normal microbiota.","zh":"“They prevent every dental infection”在此题中不正确。抗生素不能治疗病毒、消除所有风险或预防每种感染；不必要使用反而会选择耐药菌。 本题的正确原则是：不必要使用广谱抗生素会促进耐药并破坏正常菌群。"}]},{"id":"pharm-029","concept":"Antifungals & Antivirals","stem":"Nystatin is commonly used to treat:","choices":["Oral candidiasis","Herpes zoster","Bacterial endocarditis","Migraine"],"answer":0,"why":"Nystatin is a topical antifungal commonly used for oral Candida infections.","zh":"制霉菌素是常用于口腔念珠菌感染的局部抗真菌药。","pearl":"Denture and inhaler hygiene may be part of candidiasis management.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Herpes zoster” is incorrect here. Herpes zoster is caused by varicella-zoster virus and requires antiviral rather than antifungal therapy. In this question, Nystatin is a topical antifungal commonly used for oral Candida infections.","zh":"“Herpes zoster”在此题中不正确。带状疱疹由水痘-带状疱疹病毒引起，应使用抗病毒药而非抗真菌药。 本题的正确原则是：制霉菌素是常用于口腔念珠菌感染的局部抗真菌药。"},{"en":"“Bacterial endocarditis” is incorrect here. Bacterial endocarditis is a serious bacterial infection; nystatin does not treat it. In this question, Nystatin is a topical antifungal commonly used for oral Candida infections.","zh":"“Bacterial endocarditis”在此题中不正确。细菌性心内膜炎是严重细菌感染，制霉菌素不能治疗。 本题的正确原则是：制霉菌素是常用于口腔念珠菌感染的局部抗真菌药。"},{"en":"“Migraine” is incorrect here. Migraine is a neurologic headache disorder and is not an indication for nystatin. In this question, Nystatin is a topical antifungal commonly used for oral Candida infections.","zh":"“Migraine”在此题中不正确。偏头痛是神经性头痛疾病，并非制霉菌素的适应证。 本题的正确原则是：制霉菌素是常用于口腔念珠菌感染的局部抗真菌药。"}]},{"id":"pharm-030","concept":"Antifungals & Antivirals","stem":"Acyclovir and related drugs are used primarily against:","choices":["Herpes viruses","Candida species","Anaerobic bacteria","All parasites"],"answer":0,"why":"Acyclovir inhibits replication of herpes-family viruses.","zh":"阿昔洛韦类药物主要抑制疱疹病毒复制。","pearl":"Antivirals reduce replication; they do not eradicate latent herpes.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Candida species” is incorrect here. Candida are fungi and are treated with antifungals, not acyclovir. In this question, Acyclovir inhibits replication of herpes-family viruses.","zh":"“Candida species”在此题中不正确。念珠菌属于真菌，应使用抗真菌药，而非阿昔洛韦。 本题的正确原则是：阿昔洛韦类药物主要抑制疱疹病毒复制。"},{"en":"“Anaerobic bacteria” is incorrect here. Anaerobic bacterial infections require antibacterial therapy; acyclovir has antiviral activity. In this question, Acyclovir inhibits replication of herpes-family viruses.","zh":"“Anaerobic bacteria”在此题中不正确。厌氧菌感染需要抗菌治疗；阿昔洛韦具有抗病毒作用。 本题的正确原则是：阿昔洛韦类药物主要抑制疱疹病毒复制。"},{"en":"“All parasites” is incorrect here. Acyclovir is not a broad antiparasitic agent; its principal activity is against herpes viruses. In this question, Acyclovir inhibits replication of herpes-family viruses.","zh":"“All parasites”在此题中不正确。阿昔洛韦不是广谱抗寄生虫药，其主要作用对象是疱疹病毒。 本题的正确原则是：阿昔洛韦类药物主要抑制疱疹病毒复制。"}]},{"id":"pharm-031","concept":"Respiratory Drugs","stem":"A short-acting beta2 agonist inhaler such as salbutamol is used primarily for:","choices":["Rapid relief of bronchospasm","Long-term anticoagulation","Treatment of candidiasis","Control of bacterial infection"],"answer":0,"why":"Short-acting beta2 agonists provide rapid bronchodilation during acute bronchospasm.","zh":"短效β2受体激动剂可迅速扩张支气管，用于急性支气管痉挛缓解。","pearl":"Rescue inhaler = rapid relief.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Long-term anticoagulation” is incorrect here. A short-acting beta2 agonist is a rescue bronchodilator and does not treat this condition. In this question, Short-acting beta2 agonists provide rapid bronchodilation during acute bronchospasm.","zh":"“Long-term anticoagulation”在此题中不正确。短效β2激动剂是急救支气管扩张药，不能治疗该情况。 本题的正确原则是：短效β2受体激动剂可迅速扩张支气管，用于急性支气管痉挛缓解。"},{"en":"“Treatment of candidiasis” is incorrect here. A short-acting beta2 agonist is a rescue bronchodilator and does not treat this condition. In this question, Short-acting beta2 agonists provide rapid bronchodilation during acute bronchospasm.","zh":"“Treatment of candidiasis”在此题中不正确。短效β2激动剂是急救支气管扩张药，不能治疗该情况。 本题的正确原则是：短效β2受体激动剂可迅速扩张支气管，用于急性支气管痉挛缓解。"},{"en":"“Control of bacterial infection” is incorrect here. A short-acting beta2 agonist is a rescue bronchodilator and does not treat this condition. In this question, Short-acting beta2 agonists provide rapid bronchodilation during acute bronchospasm.","zh":"“Control of bacterial infection”在此题中不正确。短效β2激动剂是急救支气管扩张药，不能治疗该情况。 本题的正确原则是：短效β2受体激动剂可迅速扩张支气管，用于急性支气管痉挛缓解。"}]},{"id":"pharm-032","concept":"Respiratory Drugs","stem":"A client using an inhaled corticosteroid has recurrent oral candidiasis. Which instruction is most helpful?","choices":["Rinse the mouth after each use","Stop all asthma medication without consultation","Swallow water immediately without rinsing","Use more frequent antibiotic doses"],"answer":0,"why":"Rinsing after inhaled corticosteroids reduces residual medication and lowers candidiasis risk.","zh":"吸入糖皮质激素后漱口可减少药物残留并降低口腔念珠菌感染风险。","pearl":"Spacer use may also reduce oral deposition.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Stop all asthma medication without consultation” is incorrect here. This does not reduce local corticosteroid residue appropriately and may be unsafe or unnecessary. In this question, Rinsing after inhaled corticosteroids reduces residual medication and lowers candidiasis risk.","zh":"“Stop all asthma medication without consultation”在此题中不正确。该做法不能恰当减少局部糖皮质激素残留，且可能不安全或无必要。 本题的正确原则是：吸入糖皮质激素后漱口可减少药物残留并降低口腔念珠菌感染风险。"},{"en":"“Swallow water immediately without rinsing” is incorrect here. This does not reduce local corticosteroid residue appropriately and may be unsafe or unnecessary. In this question, Rinsing after inhaled corticosteroids reduces residual medication and lowers candidiasis risk.","zh":"“Swallow water immediately without rinsing”在此题中不正确。该做法不能恰当减少局部糖皮质激素残留，且可能不安全或无必要。 本题的正确原则是：吸入糖皮质激素后漱口可减少药物残留并降低口腔念珠菌感染风险。"},{"en":"“Use more frequent antibiotic doses” is incorrect here. This does not reduce local corticosteroid residue appropriately and may be unsafe or unnecessary. In this question, Rinsing after inhaled corticosteroids reduces residual medication and lowers candidiasis risk.","zh":"“Use more frequent antibiotic doses”在此题中不正确。该做法不能恰当减少局部糖皮质激素残留，且可能不安全或无必要。 本题的正确原则是：吸入糖皮质激素后漱口可减少药物残留并降低口腔念珠菌感染风险。"}]},{"id":"pharm-033","concept":"Diabetes Drugs","stem":"A client taking insulin becomes sweaty, shaky, and confused during care. The most likely problem is:","choices":["Hypoglycemia","Hypercalcemia","Opioid overdose","Anaphylaxis"],"answer":0,"why":"Adrenergic and neuroglycopenic symptoms such as sweating, tremor, and confusion are characteristic of hypoglycemia.","zh":"出汗、颤抖和意识混乱是低血糖常见表现。","pearl":"If conscious and able to swallow, provide fast-acting carbohydrate promptly.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Hypercalcemia” is incorrect here. Hypercalcemia does not typically present with the sudden sweating, tremor, and confusion described. In this question, Adrenergic and neuroglycopenic symptoms such as sweating, tremor, and confusion are characteristic of hypoglycemia.","zh":"“Hypercalcemia”在此题中不正确。高钙血症通常不会表现为题干所述突发出汗、发抖和意识混乱。 本题的正确原则是：出汗、颤抖和意识混乱是低血糖常见表现。"},{"en":"“Opioid overdose” is incorrect here. Opioid overdose is characterized mainly by respiratory depression, reduced consciousness, and pinpoint pupils. In this question, Adrenergic and neuroglycopenic symptoms such as sweating, tremor, and confusion are characteristic of hypoglycemia.","zh":"“Opioid overdose”在此题中不正确。阿片类药物过量主要表现为呼吸抑制、意识下降和针尖样瞳孔。 本题的正确原则是：出汗、颤抖和意识混乱是低血糖常见表现。"},{"en":"“Anaphylaxis” is incorrect here. Anaphylaxis is an acute systemic allergic reaction, usually involving airway, breathing, circulation, or skin findings. In this question, Adrenergic and neuroglycopenic symptoms such as sweating, tremor, and confusion are characteristic of hypoglycemia.","zh":"“Anaphylaxis”在此题中不正确。过敏性休克是急性全身过敏反应，常涉及气道、呼吸、循环或皮肤表现。 本题的正确原则是：出汗、颤抖和意识混乱是低血糖常见表现。"}]},{"id":"pharm-034","concept":"Diabetes Drugs","stem":"Metformin is commonly used as first-line therapy for:","choices":["Type 2 diabetes","Acute anaphylaxis","Bacterial endocarditis","Seizure termination"],"answer":0,"why":"Metformin improves insulin sensitivity and reduces hepatic glucose production in type 2 diabetes.","zh":"二甲双胍通过提高胰岛素敏感性并减少肝糖输出治疗2型糖尿病。","pearl":"Metformin alone has a relatively low hypoglycemia risk.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Acute anaphylaxis” is incorrect here. Acute anaphylaxis requires epinephrine, not metformin. In this question, Metformin improves insulin sensitivity and reduces hepatic glucose production in type 2 diabetes.","zh":"“Acute anaphylaxis”在此题中不正确。急性过敏性休克需要肾上腺素，而不是二甲双胍。 本题的正确原则是：二甲双胍通过提高胰岛素敏感性并减少肝糖输出治疗2型糖尿病。"},{"en":"“Bacterial endocarditis” is incorrect here. Bacterial endocarditis is a serious bacterial infection; nystatin does not treat it. In this question, Metformin improves insulin sensitivity and reduces hepatic glucose production in type 2 diabetes.","zh":"“Bacterial endocarditis”在此题中不正确。细菌性心内膜炎是严重细菌感染，制霉菌素不能治疗。 本题的正确原则是：二甲双胍通过提高胰岛素敏感性并减少肝糖输出治疗2型糖尿病。"},{"en":"“Seizure termination” is incorrect here. Acute seizure termination typically uses an appropriate benzodiazepine, not metformin. In this question, Metformin improves insulin sensitivity and reduces hepatic glucose production in type 2 diabetes.","zh":"“Seizure termination”在此题中不正确。急性终止癫痫发作通常使用适当的苯二氮卓类药物，而不是二甲双胍。 本题的正确原则是：二甲双胍通过提高胰岛素敏感性并减少肝糖输出治疗2型糖尿病。"}]},{"id":"pharm-035","concept":"Corticosteroids","stem":"Long-term systemic corticosteroid use may cause:","choices":["Adrenal suppression and impaired healing","Permanent bronchodilation only","Increased platelet aggregation only","Immediate tooth eruption"],"answer":0,"why":"Chronic systemic corticosteroids can suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis, impair healing, and increase infection and osteoporosis risk.","zh":"长期全身使用糖皮质激素可抑制下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺轴，并影响愈合、感染风险和骨质。","pearl":"Never assume chronic steroids can be stopped abruptly.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Permanent bronchodilation only” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Chronic systemic corticosteroids can suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis, impair healing, and increase infection and osteoporosis risk.","zh":"“Permanent bronchodilation only”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：长期全身使用糖皮质激素可抑制下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺轴，并影响愈合、感染风险和骨质。"},{"en":"“Increased platelet aggregation only” is incorrect here. This is not a recognized major consequence of long-term systemic corticosteroid exposure. In this question, Chronic systemic corticosteroids can suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis, impair healing, and increase infection and osteoporosis risk.","zh":"“Increased platelet aggregation only”在此题中不正确。这不是长期全身糖皮质激素使用的主要公认后果。 本题的正确原则是：长期全身使用糖皮质激素可抑制下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺轴，并影响愈合、感染风险和骨质。"},{"en":"“Immediate tooth eruption” is incorrect here. This is not a recognized major consequence of long-term systemic corticosteroid exposure. In this question, Chronic systemic corticosteroids can suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis, impair healing, and increase infection and osteoporosis risk.","zh":"“Immediate tooth eruption”在此题中不正确。这不是长期全身糖皮质激素使用的主要公认后果。 本题的正确原则是：长期全身使用糖皮质激素可抑制下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺轴，并影响愈合、感染风险和骨质。"}]},{"id":"pharm-036","concept":"Bone-Modifying Drugs","stem":"A key dental concern for clients receiving potent antiresorptive drugs is:","choices":["Medication-related osteonecrosis of the jaw","Immediate enamel hypoplasia","Universal anaphylaxis","Acute viral infection"],"answer":0,"why":"Bisphosphonates and other potent antiresorptives are associated with medication-related osteonecrosis of the jaw, especially with higher-dose cancer regimens and invasive procedures.","zh":"双膦酸盐等强效抗骨吸收药与药物相关性颌骨坏死有关，尤其在肿瘤高剂量方案及侵入性操作时。","pearl":"Risk depends on drug, dose, route, duration, comorbidities, and procedure.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Immediate enamel hypoplasia” is incorrect here. This is not the classic oral adverse effect associated with calcium channel blockers. In this question, Bisphosphonates and other potent antiresorptives are associated with medication-related osteonecrosis of the jaw, especially with higher-dose cancer regimens and invasive procedures.","zh":"“Immediate enamel hypoplasia”在此题中不正确。这不是钙通道阻滞剂的经典口腔不良反应。 本题的正确原则是：双膦酸盐等强效抗骨吸收药与药物相关性颌骨坏死有关，尤其在肿瘤高剂量方案及侵入性操作时。"},{"en":"“Universal anaphylaxis” is incorrect here. Anaphylaxis is an acute systemic allergic reaction, usually involving airway, breathing, circulation, or skin findings. In this question, Bisphosphonates and other potent antiresorptives are associated with medication-related osteonecrosis of the jaw, especially with higher-dose cancer regimens and invasive procedures.","zh":"“Universal anaphylaxis”在此题中不正确。过敏性休克是急性全身过敏反应，常涉及气道、呼吸、循环或皮肤表现。 本题的正确原则是：双膦酸盐等强效抗骨吸收药与药物相关性颌骨坏死有关，尤其在肿瘤高剂量方案及侵入性操作时。"},{"en":"“Acute viral infection” is incorrect here. This is not the distinctive jaw-related complication associated with potent antiresorptive therapy. In this question, Bisphosphonates and other potent antiresorptives are associated with medication-related osteonecrosis of the jaw, especially with higher-dose cancer regimens and invasive procedures.","zh":"“Acute viral infection”在此题中不正确。这不是强效抗骨吸收治疗具有特征性的颌骨并发症。 本题的正确原则是：双膦酸盐等强效抗骨吸收药与药物相关性颌骨坏死有关，尤其在肿瘤高剂量方案及侵入性操作时。"}]},{"id":"pharm-037","concept":"Bone-Modifying Drugs","stem":"What is the best preventive principle before initiating high-dose antiresorptive therapy?","choices":["Complete necessary dental assessment and stabilize oral disease when feasible","Avoid all oral hygiene","Extract every tooth","Begin elective surgery after therapy starts"],"answer":0,"why":"Pre-treatment dental assessment and management of active disease can reduce later invasive treatment needs.","zh":"在开始高剂量抗骨吸收治疗前，尽可能完成牙科评估并控制活动性口腔疾病，可减少后续侵入性治疗需求。","pearl":"Prevention is easier than managing MRONJ.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Avoid all oral hygiene” is incorrect here. Orally swallowed drugs commonly pass through the liver before reaching systemic circulation. In this question, Pre-treatment dental assessment and management of active disease can reduce later invasive treatment needs.","zh":"“Avoid all oral hygiene”在此题中不正确。口服吞咽药物通常在进入体循环前先经过肝脏。 本题的正确原则是：在开始高剂量抗骨吸收治疗前，尽可能完成牙科评估并控制活动性口腔疾病，可减少后续侵入性治疗需求。"},{"en":"“Extract every tooth” is incorrect here. This is unnecessarily harmful or increases risk; prevention focuses on assessment and stabilizing disease before therapy when feasible. In this question, Pre-treatment dental assessment and management of active disease can reduce later invasive treatment needs.","zh":"“Extract every tooth”在此题中不正确。该做法不必要且可能增加风险；预防重点是在可行时于治疗前评估并稳定口腔疾病。 本题的正确原则是：在开始高剂量抗骨吸收治疗前，尽可能完成牙科评估并控制活动性口腔疾病，可减少后续侵入性治疗需求。"},{"en":"“Begin elective surgery after therapy starts” is incorrect here. This is unnecessarily harmful or increases risk; prevention focuses on assessment and stabilizing disease before therapy when feasible. In this question, Pre-treatment dental assessment and management of active disease can reduce later invasive treatment needs.","zh":"“Begin elective surgery after therapy starts”在此题中不正确。该做法不必要且可能增加风险；预防重点是在可行时于治疗前评估并稳定口腔疾病。 本题的正确原则是：在开始高剂量抗骨吸收治疗前，尽可能完成牙科评估并控制活动性口腔疾病，可减少后续侵入性治疗需求。"}]},{"id":"pharm-038","concept":"Local Anesthetics","stem":"Local anesthetics primarily prevent nerve conduction by blocking:","choices":["Voltage-gated sodium channels","Calcium absorption from the gut","Histamine receptors","Cyclooxygenase only"],"answer":0,"why":"Local anesthetics block voltage-gated sodium channels, preventing action-potential propagation.","zh":"局部麻醉药通过阻断电压门控钠通道，阻止动作电位传导。","pearl":"No sodium influx, no nerve impulse.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Calcium absorption from the gut” is incorrect here. Absorption is entry of a drug from the administration site into systemic circulation. In this question, Local anesthetics block voltage-gated sodium channels, preventing action-potential propagation.","zh":"“Calcium absorption from the gut”在此题中不正确。吸收是药物从给药部位进入体循环。 本题的正确原则是：局部麻醉药通过阻断电压门控钠通道，阻止动作电位传导。"},{"en":"“Histamine receptors” is incorrect here. Histamine-receptor blockade is the mechanism of antihistamines, not local anesthetics. In this question, Local anesthetics block voltage-gated sodium channels, preventing action-potential propagation.","zh":"“Histamine receptors”在此题中不正确。阻断组胺受体是抗组胺药的机制，并非局部麻醉药的机制。 本题的正确原则是：局部麻醉药通过阻断电压门控钠通道，阻止动作电位传导。"},{"en":"“Cyclooxygenase only” is incorrect here. This option describes a different condition, drug action, or clinical use and does not match the mechanism or safety issue tested here. In this question, Local anesthetics block voltage-gated sodium channels, preventing action-potential propagation.","zh":"“Cyclooxygenase only”在此题中不正确。该选项描述的是不同的疾病、药物作用或临床用途，与本题考查的机制或安全问题不符。 本题的正确原则是：局部麻醉药通过阻断电压门控钠通道，阻止动作电位传导。"}]},{"id":"pharm-039","concept":"Local Anesthetics","stem":"Why is a vasoconstrictor added to some local anesthetic solutions?","choices":["To slow systemic absorption and prolong local action","To cause immediate general anesthesia","To eliminate all toxicity","To treat candidiasis"],"answer":0,"why":"Local vasoconstriction reduces blood flow, slows systemic uptake, and prolongs anesthetic effect.","zh":"血管收缩剂可减少局部血流、减慢全身吸收并延长麻醉作用。","pearl":"Vasoconstrictor improves duration but requires patient-specific caution.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“To cause immediate general anesthesia” is incorrect here. A vasoconstrictor does not accomplish this; it reduces local blood flow, slows absorption, and prolongs anesthesia. In this question, Local vasoconstriction reduces blood flow, slows systemic uptake, and prolongs anesthetic effect.","zh":"“To cause immediate general anesthesia”在此题中不正确。血管收缩剂不能达到该目的；其作用是减少局部血流、减慢吸收并延长麻醉。 本题的正确原则是：血管收缩剂可减少局部血流、减慢全身吸收并延长麻醉作用。"},{"en":"“To eliminate all toxicity” is incorrect here. A vasoconstrictor does not accomplish this; it reduces local blood flow, slows absorption, and prolongs anesthesia. In this question, Local vasoconstriction reduces blood flow, slows systemic uptake, and prolongs anesthetic effect.","zh":"“To eliminate all toxicity”在此题中不正确。血管收缩剂不能达到该目的；其作用是减少局部血流、减慢吸收并延长麻醉。 本题的正确原则是：血管收缩剂可减少局部血流、减慢全身吸收并延长麻醉作用。"},{"en":"“To treat candidiasis” is incorrect here. A short-acting beta2 agonist is a rescue bronchodilator and does not treat this condition. In this question, Local vasoconstriction reduces blood flow, slows systemic uptake, and prolongs anesthetic effect.","zh":"“To treat candidiasis”在此题中不正确。短效β2激动剂是急救支气管扩张药，不能治疗该情况。 本题的正确原则是：血管收缩剂可减少局部血流、减慢全身吸收并延长麻醉作用。"}]},{"id":"pharm-040","concept":"Local Anesthetics","stem":"Which early symptom may suggest local anesthetic systemic toxicity?","choices":["Circumoral numbness, tinnitus, or metallic taste","Gingival enlargement months later","Chronic candidiasis only","Slow nail growth"],"answer":0,"why":"Early CNS toxicity can include circumoral numbness, tinnitus, metallic taste, dizziness, or agitation before seizures or cardiovascular effects.","zh":"局麻药全身毒性早期可出现口周麻木、耳鸣、金属味、头晕或躁动。","pearl":"Recognize early neurologic warning signs.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Gingival enlargement months later” is incorrect here. This is not the principal toxicity produced by excessive acetaminophen exposure. In this question, Early CNS toxicity can include circumoral numbness, tinnitus, metallic taste, dizziness, or agitation before seizures or cardiovascular effects.","zh":"“Gingival enlargement months later”在此题中不正确。这不是过量对乙酰氨基酚的主要毒性表现。 本题的正确原则是：局麻药全身毒性早期可出现口周麻木、耳鸣、金属味、头晕或躁动。"},{"en":"“Chronic candidiasis only” is incorrect here. A short-acting beta2 agonist is a rescue bronchodilator and does not treat this condition. In this question, Early CNS toxicity can include circumoral numbness, tinnitus, metallic taste, dizziness, or agitation before seizures or cardiovascular effects.","zh":"“Chronic candidiasis only”在此题中不正确。短效β2激动剂是急救支气管扩张药，不能治疗该情况。 本题的正确原则是：局麻药全身毒性早期可出现口周麻木、耳鸣、金属味、头晕或躁动。"},{"en":"“Slow nail growth” is incorrect here. This is not an early neurologic warning sign of local-anesthetic systemic toxicity. In this question, Early CNS toxicity can include circumoral numbness, tinnitus, metallic taste, dizziness, or agitation before seizures or cardiovascular effects.","zh":"“Slow nail growth”在此题中不正确。这不是局部麻醉药全身毒性的早期神经系统警示症状。 本题的正确原则是：局麻药全身毒性早期可出现口周麻木、耳鸣、金属味、头晕或躁动。"}]},{"id":"pharm-041","concept":"Drug Interactions","stem":"A client takes multiple medications from several prescribers. What is the best dental hygiene action?","choices":["Reconcile all medications, indications, doses, and relevant interactions","Review only antibiotics","Assume over-the-counter products do not matter","Ask the client to stop everything"],"answer":0,"why":"Medication reconciliation includes prescription, nonprescription, herbal, and recreational substances because all may affect care.","zh":"药物核对应包括处方药、非处方药、草药和娱乐性物质，因为都可能影响护理。","pearl":"A medication list without indication and dose is only half a map.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Review only antibiotics” is incorrect here. It produces an incomplete or unsafe medication assessment; all prescribed, nonprescription, and relevant natural products matter. In this question, Medication reconciliation includes prescription, nonprescription, herbal, and recreational substances because all may affect care.","zh":"“Review only antibiotics”在此题中不正确。该做法会造成不完整或不安全的用药评估；处方药、非处方药和相关天然产品都需考虑。 本题的正确原则是：药物核对应包括处方药、非处方药、草药和娱乐性物质，因为都可能影响护理。"},{"en":"“Assume over-the-counter products do not matter” is incorrect here. It produces an incomplete or unsafe medication assessment; all prescribed, nonprescription, and relevant natural products matter. In this question, Medication reconciliation includes prescription, nonprescription, herbal, and recreational substances because all may affect care.","zh":"“Assume over-the-counter products do not matter”在此题中不正确。该做法会造成不完整或不安全的用药评估；处方药、非处方药和相关天然产品都需考虑。 本题的正确原则是：药物核对应包括处方药、非处方药、草药和娱乐性物质，因为都可能影响护理。"},{"en":"“Ask the client to stop everything” is incorrect here. It produces an incomplete or unsafe medication assessment; all prescribed, nonprescription, and relevant natural products matter. In this question, Medication reconciliation includes prescription, nonprescription, herbal, and recreational substances because all may affect care.","zh":"“Ask the client to stop everything”在此题中不正确。该做法会造成不完整或不安全的用药评估；处方药、非处方药和相关天然产品都需考虑。 本题的正确原则是：药物核对应包括处方药、非处方药、草药和娱乐性物质，因为都可能影响护理。"}]},{"id":"pharm-042","concept":"Drug Interactions","stem":"Why can combining several drugs with anticholinergic effects be clinically important?","choices":["Their dry-mouth and other anticholinergic effects may be additive","They always cancel each other","They prevent caries","They eliminate urinary retention"],"answer":0,"why":"Anticholinergic burden can accumulate, increasing xerostomia, blurred vision, constipation, urinary retention, and confusion.","zh":"多种抗胆碱能药物的作用可叠加，增加口干、视物模糊、便秘、尿潴留和意识混乱。","pearl":"Think cumulative burden, especially in older adults.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“They always cancel each other” is incorrect here. Anticholinergic effects are additive, so this claim reverses or ignores the expected pharmacology. In this question, Anticholinergic burden can accumulate, increasing xerostomia, blurred vision, constipation, urinary retention, and confusion.","zh":"“They always cancel each other”在此题中不正确。抗胆碱作用可以叠加，因此该说法颠倒或忽略了预期药理效应。 本题的正确原则是：多种抗胆碱能药物的作用可叠加，增加口干、视物模糊、便秘、尿潴留和意识混乱。"},{"en":"“They prevent caries” is incorrect here. Anticholinergic effects are additive, so this claim reverses or ignores the expected pharmacology. In this question, Anticholinergic burden can accumulate, increasing xerostomia, blurred vision, constipation, urinary retention, and confusion.","zh":"“They prevent caries”在此题中不正确。抗胆碱作用可以叠加，因此该说法颠倒或忽略了预期药理效应。 本题的正确原则是：多种抗胆碱能药物的作用可叠加，增加口干、视物模糊、便秘、尿潴留和意识混乱。"},{"en":"“They eliminate urinary retention” is incorrect here. Anticholinergic effects are additive, so this claim reverses or ignores the expected pharmacology. In this question, Anticholinergic burden can accumulate, increasing xerostomia, blurred vision, constipation, urinary retention, and confusion.","zh":"“They eliminate urinary retention”在此题中不正确。抗胆碱作用可以叠加，因此该说法颠倒或忽略了预期药理效应。 本题的正确原则是：多种抗胆碱能药物的作用可叠加，增加口干、视物模糊、便秘、尿潴留和意识混乱。"}]},{"id":"pharm-043","concept":"Psychotropic Drugs","stem":"Which oral effect is common with many antidepressants?","choices":["Xerostomia","Permanent enamel regeneration","Profuse salivation in every client","Immediate gingival necrosis"],"answer":0,"why":"Many antidepressants have anticholinergic or related effects that reduce salivary flow.","zh":"许多抗抑郁药具有抗胆碱能或类似作用，可减少唾液分泌。","pearl":"Dry mouth changes caries risk, comfort, swallowing, and adherence.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Permanent enamel regeneration” is incorrect here. This is not a common oral effect of antidepressant therapy. In this question, Many antidepressants have anticholinergic or related effects that reduce salivary flow.","zh":"“Permanent enamel regeneration”在此题中不正确。这不是抗抑郁药治疗的常见口腔效应。 本题的正确原则是：许多抗抑郁药具有抗胆碱能或类似作用，可减少唾液分泌。"},{"en":"“Profuse salivation in every client” is incorrect here. This is not a common oral effect of antidepressant therapy. In this question, Many antidepressants have anticholinergic or related effects that reduce salivary flow.","zh":"“Profuse salivation in every client”在此题中不正确。这不是抗抑郁药治疗的常见口腔效应。 本题的正确原则是：许多抗抑郁药具有抗胆碱能或类似作用，可减少唾液分泌。"},{"en":"“Immediate gingival necrosis” is incorrect here. This is not a common oral effect of antidepressant therapy. In this question, Many antidepressants have anticholinergic or related effects that reduce salivary flow.","zh":"“Immediate gingival necrosis”在此题中不正确。这不是抗抑郁药治疗的常见口腔效应。 本题的正确原则是：许多抗抑郁药具有抗胆碱能或类似作用，可减少唾液分泌。"}]},{"id":"pharm-044","concept":"Psychotropic Drugs","stem":"A client taking a monoamine oxidase inhibitor requires careful review before receiving:","choices":["Sympathomimetic drugs","Topical fluoride","Plain water","A toothbrush"],"answer":0,"why":"MAO inhibitors can interact dangerously with sympathomimetic agents and several other drugs, producing hypertensive or serotonergic complications.","zh":"单胺氧化酶抑制剂可与拟交感药及多种其他药物发生严重相互作用，引起高血压或血清素相关并发症。","pearl":"MAOI on the history should trigger interaction checking.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Topical fluoride” is incorrect here. Topical fluoride acts locally to prevent caries and is not a sympathomimetic interaction concern. In this question, MAO inhibitors can interact dangerously with sympathomimetic agents and several other drugs, producing hypertensive or serotonergic complications.","zh":"“Topical fluoride”在此题中不正确。局部氟化物用于局部防龋，并非拟交感神经药相互作用问题。 本题的正确原则是：单胺氧化酶抑制剂可与拟交感药及多种其他药物发生严重相互作用，引起高血压或血清素相关并发症。"},{"en":"“Plain water” is incorrect here. Plain water has no sympathomimetic drug action. In this question, MAO inhibitors can interact dangerously with sympathomimetic agents and several other drugs, producing hypertensive or serotonergic complications.","zh":"“Plain water”在此题中不正确。清水没有拟交感神经药理作用。 本题的正确原则是：单胺氧化酶抑制剂可与拟交感药及多种其他药物发生严重相互作用，引起高血压或血清素相关并发症。"},{"en":"“A toothbrush” is incorrect here. A toothbrush is not a medication and does not create a monoamine oxidase inhibitor interaction. In this question, MAO inhibitors can interact dangerously with sympathomimetic agents and several other drugs, producing hypertensive or serotonergic complications.","zh":"“A toothbrush”在此题中不正确。牙刷不是药物，不会与单胺氧化酶抑制剂发生药物相互作用。 本题的正确原则是：单胺氧化酶抑制剂可与拟交感药及多种其他药物发生严重相互作用，引起高血压或血清素相关并发症。"}]},{"id":"pharm-045","concept":"Emergency Medications","stem":"Epinephrine is the first-line medication for:","choices":["Anaphylaxis","Simple fainting after recovery","Oral candidiasis","Chronic gingivitis"],"answer":0,"why":"Epinephrine rapidly treats airway edema, bronchospasm, and circulatory collapse in anaphylaxis.","zh":"肾上腺素可迅速改善过敏性休克中的气道水肿、支气管痉挛和循环衰竭。","pearl":"Anaphylaxis: epinephrine first, not an antihistamine first.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Simple fainting after recovery” is incorrect here. Epinephrine is not first-line treatment for this condition. In this question, Epinephrine rapidly treats airway edema, bronchospasm, and circulatory collapse in anaphylaxis.","zh":"“Simple fainting after recovery”在此题中不正确。肾上腺素不是该情况的一线治疗药物。 本题的正确原则是：肾上腺素可迅速改善过敏性休克中的气道水肿、支气管痉挛和循环衰竭。"},{"en":"“Oral candidiasis” is incorrect here. Oral candidiasis is a fungal Candida infection and is appropriately treated with antifungals such as nystatin. In this question, Epinephrine rapidly treats airway edema, bronchospasm, and circulatory collapse in anaphylaxis.","zh":"“Oral candidiasis”在此题中不正确。口腔念珠菌病是真菌感染，可用制霉菌素等抗真菌药治疗。 本题的正确原则是：肾上腺素可迅速改善过敏性休克中的气道水肿、支气管痉挛和循环衰竭。"},{"en":"“Chronic gingivitis” is incorrect here. Epinephrine is not first-line treatment for this condition. In this question, Epinephrine rapidly treats airway edema, bronchospasm, and circulatory collapse in anaphylaxis.","zh":"“Chronic gingivitis”在此题中不正确。肾上腺素不是该情况的一线治疗药物。 本题的正确原则是：肾上腺素可迅速改善过敏性休克中的气道水肿、支气管痉挛和循环衰竭。"}]},{"id":"pharm-046","concept":"Emergency Medications","stem":"Nitroglycerin is used in the dental setting primarily for a client with:","choices":["Suspected angina when appropriate and not contraindicated","Hypoglycemia","Anaphylaxis","Seizure activity"],"answer":0,"why":"Nitroglycerin is a vasodilator used for anginal chest pain when the client's status and contraindications permit.","zh":"硝酸甘油是一种血管扩张剂，可在无禁忌且情况适当时用于心绞痛性胸痛。","pearl":"Chest pain that does not resolve promptly may represent myocardial infarction.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Hypoglycemia” is incorrect here. Hypoglycemia causes adrenergic and neuroglycopenic signs such as sweating, shaking, and confusion. In this question, Nitroglycerin is a vasodilator used for anginal chest pain when the client's status and contraindications permit.","zh":"“Hypoglycemia”在此题中不正确。低血糖可引起出汗、发抖、意识混乱等交感神经和神经缺糖症状。 本题的正确原则是：硝酸甘油是一种血管扩张剂，可在无禁忌且情况适当时用于心绞痛性胸痛。"},{"en":"“Anaphylaxis” is incorrect here. Anaphylaxis is an acute systemic allergic reaction, usually involving airway, breathing, circulation, or skin findings. In this question, Nitroglycerin is a vasodilator used for anginal chest pain when the client's status and contraindications permit.","zh":"“Anaphylaxis”在此题中不正确。过敏性休克是急性全身过敏反应，常涉及气道、呼吸、循环或皮肤表现。 本题的正确原则是：硝酸甘油是一种血管扩张剂，可在无禁忌且情况适当时用于心绞痛性胸痛。"},{"en":"“Seizure activity” is incorrect here. Nitroglycerin treats ischemic chest pain and is not the primary medication for this emergency. In this question, Nitroglycerin is a vasodilator used for anginal chest pain when the client's status and contraindications permit.","zh":"“Seizure activity”在此题中不正确。硝酸甘油用于缺血性胸痛，并非该急症的主要用药。 本题的正确原则是：硝酸甘油是一种血管扩张剂，可在无禁忌且情况适当时用于心绞痛性胸痛。"}]},{"id":"pharm-047","concept":"Oral Adverse Effects","stem":"Which medication-related condition increases caries risk most directly?","choices":["Xerostomia","Mild transient headache","Bradycardia alone","Myalgia alone"],"answer":0,"why":"Reduced salivary flow diminishes buffering, cleansing, remineralization, and antimicrobial protection.","zh":"唾液减少会削弱缓冲、清洁、再矿化和抗菌保护，从而增加龋病风险。","pearl":"Medication-induced dry mouth deserves preventive care, not just reassurance.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Mild transient headache” is incorrect here. This may be clinically relevant, but it does not increase caries risk as directly as reduced salivary protection. In this question, Reduced salivary flow diminishes buffering, cleansing, remineralization, and antimicrobial protection.","zh":"“Mild transient headache”在此题中不正确。该情况可能有临床意义，但不像唾液保护减少那样直接增加龋病风险。 本题的正确原则是：唾液减少会削弱缓冲、清洁、再矿化和抗菌保护，从而增加龋病风险。"},{"en":"“Bradycardia alone” is incorrect here. This may be clinically relevant, but it does not increase caries risk as directly as reduced salivary protection. In this question, Reduced salivary flow diminishes buffering, cleansing, remineralization, and antimicrobial protection.","zh":"“Bradycardia alone”在此题中不正确。该情况可能有临床意义，但不像唾液保护减少那样直接增加龋病风险。 本题的正确原则是：唾液减少会削弱缓冲、清洁、再矿化和抗菌保护，从而增加龋病风险。"},{"en":"“Myalgia alone” is incorrect here. This may be clinically relevant, but it does not increase caries risk as directly as reduced salivary protection. In this question, Reduced salivary flow diminishes buffering, cleansing, remineralization, and antimicrobial protection.","zh":"“Myalgia alone”在此题中不正确。该情况可能有临床意义，但不像唾液保护减少那样直接增加龋病风险。 本题的正确原则是：唾液减少会削弱缓冲、清洁、再矿化和抗菌保护，从而增加龋病风险。"}]},{"id":"pharm-048","concept":"Clinical Case","stem":"A client takes warfarin, reports a new antibiotic prescription, and has not had a recent INR. What is the best approach before invasive instrumentation?","choices":["Proceed without review","Assess the antibiotic interaction potential, bleeding history, and current anticoagulation information; consult when indicated","Tell the client to omit warfarin for three days","Replace warfarin with aspirin"],"answer":1,"why":"Some antibiotics can alter warfarin effect. The clinician should evaluate current information and coordinate care rather than independently changing therapy.","zh":"部分抗生素会影响华法林作用。应评估相互作用、出血史和当前抗凝情况，并在需要时会诊，而不是自行更改治疗。","pearl":"New drugs can destabilize previously stable anticoagulation.","rationales":[{"en":"“Proceed without review” is incorrect here. Ignoring anticoagulation can miss clinically important bleeding and drug-interaction risks. In this question, Some antibiotics can alter warfarin effect. The clinician should evaluate current information and coordinate care rather than independently changing therapy.","zh":"“Proceed without review”在此题中不正确。忽视抗凝治疗会漏掉重要出血和药物相互作用风险。 本题的正确原则是：部分抗生素会影响华法林作用。应评估相互作用、出血史和当前抗凝情况，并在需要时会诊，而不是自行更改治疗。"},{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Tell the client to omit warfarin for three days” is incorrect here. Anticoagulant therapy should not be independently changed by the dental hygienist; risk assessment and consultation are required when indicated. In this question, Some antibiotics can alter warfarin effect. The clinician should evaluate current information and coordinate care rather than independently changing therapy.","zh":"“Tell the client to omit warfarin for three days”在此题中不正确。牙科保健师不应自行更改抗凝治疗；应评估风险并在需要时会诊。 本题的正确原则是：部分抗生素会影响华法林作用。应评估相互作用、出血史和当前抗凝情况，并在需要时会诊，而不是自行更改治疗。"},{"en":"“Replace warfarin with aspirin” is incorrect here. Aspirin irreversibly inhibits platelet cyclooxygenase for the platelet's lifespan. In this question, Some antibiotics can alter warfarin effect. The clinician should evaluate current information and coordinate care rather than independently changing therapy.","zh":"“Replace warfarin with aspirin”在此题中不正确。阿司匹林不可逆抑制血小板环氧化酶，作用持续至血小板寿命结束。 本题的正确原则是：部分抗生素会影响华法林作用。应评估相互作用、出血史和当前抗凝情况，并在需要时会诊，而不是自行更改治疗。"}]},{"id":"pharm-049","concept":"Clinical Case","stem":"A client with asthma uses salbutamol several times daily and has no controller medication. What is the most appropriate interpretation?","choices":["Asthma may be poorly controlled and requires medical follow-up","This proves the asthma is cured","The inhaler should be discarded","No relevance to dental care"],"answer":0,"why":"Frequent rescue-inhaler use suggests inadequate control and greater risk of an acute episode during care.","zh":"频繁使用急救吸入剂提示哮喘控制不佳，治疗期间发生急性发作的风险更高。","pearl":"Frequency of rescue use is a control clue.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“This proves the asthma is cured” is incorrect here. Frequent rescue-inhaler use suggests poor control rather than cure and is relevant to dental risk assessment. In this question, Frequent rescue-inhaler use suggests inadequate control and greater risk of an acute episode during care.","zh":"“This proves the asthma is cured”在此题中不正确。频繁使用急救吸入剂提示控制不佳而非治愈，并且与牙科风险评估有关。 本题的正确原则是：频繁使用急救吸入剂提示哮喘控制不佳，治疗期间发生急性发作的风险更高。"},{"en":"“The inhaler should be discarded” is incorrect here. Frequent rescue-inhaler use suggests poor control rather than cure and is relevant to dental risk assessment. In this question, Frequent rescue-inhaler use suggests inadequate control and greater risk of an acute episode during care.","zh":"“The inhaler should be discarded”在此题中不正确。频繁使用急救吸入剂提示控制不佳而非治愈，并且与牙科风险评估有关。 本题的正确原则是：频繁使用急救吸入剂提示哮喘控制不佳，治疗期间发生急性发作的风险更高。"},{"en":"“No relevance to dental care” is incorrect here. Frequent rescue-inhaler use suggests poor control rather than cure and is relevant to dental risk assessment. In this question, Frequent rescue-inhaler use suggests inadequate control and greater risk of an acute episode during care.","zh":"“No relevance to dental care”在此题中不正确。频繁使用急救吸入剂提示控制不佳而非治愈，并且与牙科风险评估有关。 本题的正确原则是：频繁使用急救吸入剂提示哮喘控制不佳，治疗期间发生急性发作的风险更高。"}]},{"id":"pharm-050","concept":"Clinical Case","stem":"A client taking several xerogenic medications has root caries and difficulty swallowing dry foods. Which plan is best?","choices":["Review medications and indications, assess salivary function, intensify fluoride and caries prevention, and coordinate care when appropriate","Tell the client to stop every medication","Recommend sugary lozenges continuously","Ignore the symptoms"],"answer":0,"why":"Management should address causes, oral consequences, symptom relief, and prevention without independently discontinuing essential medications.","zh":"处理应包括评估药物原因和唾液功能、加强氟化物与龋病预防，并在适当时协调医疗护理，而不是自行停药。","pearl":"Treat xerostomia as a risk condition, not merely a comfort complaint.","rationales":[{"en":"This is the best answer because it matches the pharmacologic principle explained above.","zh":"这是最佳答案，因为它符合上方解释的药理原则。"},{"en":"“Tell the client to stop every medication” is incorrect here. This is unsafe or increases caries risk and fails to manage medication-related salivary dysfunction collaboratively. In this question, Management should address causes, oral consequences, symptom relief, and prevention without independently discontinuing essential medications.","zh":"“Tell the client to stop every medication”在此题中不正确。该做法不安全或会增加龋病风险，也未能协作处理药物相关唾液功能障碍。 本题的正确原则是：处理应包括评估药物原因和唾液功能、加强氟化物与龋病预防，并在适当时协调医疗护理，而不是自行停药。"},{"en":"“Recommend sugary lozenges continuously” is incorrect here. This is unsafe or increases caries risk and fails to manage medication-related salivary dysfunction collaboratively. In this question, Management should address causes, oral consequences, symptom relief, and prevention without independently discontinuing essential medications.","zh":"“Recommend sugary lozenges continuously”在此题中不正确。该做法不安全或会增加龋病风险，也未能协作处理药物相关唾液功能障碍。 本题的正确原则是：处理应包括评估药物原因和唾液功能、加强氟化物与龋病预防，并在适当时协调医疗护理，而不是自行停药。"},{"en":"“Ignore the symptoms” is incorrect here. This is unsafe or increases caries risk and fails to manage medication-related salivary dysfunction collaboratively. In this question, Management should address causes, oral consequences, symptom relief, and prevention without independently discontinuing essential medications.","zh":"“Ignore the symptoms”在此题中不正确。该做法不安全或会增加龋病风险，也未能协作处理药物相关唾液功能障碍。 本题的正确原则是：处理应包括评估药物原因和唾液功能、加强氟化物与龋病预防，并在适当时协调医疗护理，而不是自行停药。"}]}];